==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|heben}}, {{m|gmh|heven}} (rarer {{m|gmh|heffen}}), from {{inh|de|goh|heffen}}, {{m|goh|heven}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*haffjan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*hafjaną}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*kh₂pyé-}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*keh₂p-||to seize}}. Compare {{cog|nl|heffen}}, {{cog|en|heave}}, {{cog|da|hæve}}. {{doublet|de|hieven}}.

The ''-b-'' is regular in the past tense and participle. In Middle High German the paradigm was regularised by spreading ''-b-'' to the present tense; ''-f-'' is preserved in related {{m|de|Hefe|t=yeast}}. The past forms were originally {{m|de|hub}}, {{m|de|gehaben}}, still retained in Early Modern German. The verb was then shifted to the class of {{m|de|fliegen}} etc. (Compare {{m+|nl|heffen}}, which was also shifted, though to a different ablaut class.)

